OL,3,GNEWSA'With London in drought we need to
OL,4,Achange how we think about water'
OL,5,
OL,6,FHyde Park looks more like the Serengeti
OL,7,Fand the green belt has turned yellow.
OL,8,FBut with London now seeing the
OL,9,Foccasional shower, does that mean we
OL,10,Fare no longer in drought? And if not,
OL,11,Fthe big question is how long will the
OL,12,Fdrought last?
OL,14,FThe capital is particularly susceptible
OL,15,Fto drought as there is a very large
OL,16,Fpopulation, in an area that is actually
OL,17,Fvery dry. Experts call it "water
OL,18,Fstressed."
OL,20,FThe myth is London is a rainy city, yet
OL,21,Fthe capital gets less rain than many
OL,22,Fother cities in Europe.
OL,23,APub: 25-AugQppppppppppppppppppppppG1/2
OL,24,ANext PageBLon/SE NewsCReg TVFClean Feed
FL,326,320,200,140,0,100
